    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0718" n="2182" xml:id="pg2182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Henderson, Loy W.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in India
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-14T13:00:00-04:00">September 14,
                            1951—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>607. For Henderson from McGhee. If you have not yet paid farewell call on
                        Nehru<anchor n="1" xml:id="d484-f1"/> you may wish consider conveying to him
                    as departing friend your forthright personal observations on possible
                    consequences to India if GOI fols present course
                    in fon relations. I leave to ur discretion the forcefulness with which you may
                    wish to present ur views. I am sure you will agree this occasion may offer an
                    opportunity to obtain from Nehru rather more realistic and comprehensive views
                    than he has heretofore expressed. [McGhee.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d484-f1" n="1" xml:id="d484-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Henderson was appointed Ambassador to Iran effective September 19; he
                    departed from New Delhi on September 21.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
